# fullrust support for rustix 1.1.5 — run rustix's own raw-syscall `linux_raw`
# backend, unmodified, on the libc-free Linux-ABI target (auto-selected, no
# rustflags, no libc/errno in the graph).
# Applied on top of crates.io rustix 1.1.5 (vendored in crates/rustix/).
#
# Why a fork is unavoidable: rustix's build.rs picks the backend with
# `os != "linux"` -> libc (no cfg/feature overrides that), Cargo.toml pulls
# `libc`+`errno` for any non-Linux OS, and the linux_raw backend itself relies
# on items gated `target_os = "linux"` / `unix`. Neither `--cfg linux_raw`
# nor `--cfg target_os="linux"` in RUSTFLAGS gets a pristine rustix to build.
#
# The diff is purely mechanical (regenerate on a new upstream release by
# re-applying these rules):
#  1. build.rs: `os == "fullrust"` is treated as `os == "linux"` (-> linux_raw,
#     linux_kernel, linux_like); `use-libc` is ignored on fullrust.
#  2. Cargo.toml: the linux_raw `linux-raw-sys` table and the two
#     "not Linux => libc/errno" tables also match `target_os = "fullrust"`
#     (the optional libc/libc_errno of `use-libc` stay Linux-only).
#  3. src/ (excluding backend/libc): every `target_os = "linux"` ->
#     `any(target_os = "linux", target_os = "fullrust")`.
#  4. src/ cfg attributes (excluding backend/libc and the 4 files below):
#     bare `unix` -> `any(unix, target_os = "fullrust")` (AF_UNIX addresses,
#     the no_std fd polyfill).
#  5. std paths that name `std::os::unix`: fullrust gets the same items from
#     `std::os::fd` (maybe_polyfill/std) and `std::os::fullrust::ffi`
#     (path/arg.rs, path/dec_int.rs). `rustix::fs::{FileExt, MetadataExt, ..}`
#     (re-exports of std::os::unix::fs) are simply absent on fullrust.

